00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The Bourne Supremacy is a 2004 American action-thriller film
featuring Robert Ludlum's Jason Bourne character.

12
00:58:54,545 --> 00:59:00,545
Although it takes the name of the second Bourne novel
(1986), its plot is entirely different.

13
01:03:49,090 --> 01:03:55,090
The film was directed by Paul Greengrass from a screenplay by Tony Gilroy.

14
01:08:43,636 --> 01:08:49,636
The second installment in the Bourne film series after The Bourne Identity (2002), it stars Matt
Damon as Jason Bourne, a former CIA assassin suffering from psychogenic amnesia.

15
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
In the film, Bourne is attempting to learn more of his past as he is once more
enveloped in a conspiracy involving the CIA and Operation Treadstone.

16
01:18:32,727 --> 01:18:38,727
Actors Franka Potente, Brian Cox, Gabriel Mann, and Julia Stiles reprise their roles as
Marie Kreutz, Ward Abbott, Danny Zorn and Nicky Parsons, respectively.

17
01:23:27,272 --> 01:23:33,272
Karl Urban and Joan Allen join the cast as Kirill
and Pamela Landy, respectively.

18
01:28:21,818 --> 01:28:27,818
The Bourne Supremacy premiered at the ArcLight Hollywood on July 15, 2004, and was theatrically released in the United States on July 23, by
Universal Pictures It received positive reviews and was a commercial success, grossing $290 million on a $75 million budget.

19
01:33:16,363 --> 01:33:22,363
The film was followed by The Bourne Ultimatum (2007), The
Bourne Legacy (2012), and Jason Bourne (2016).

20
01:38:10,909 --> 01:38:16,909
The film explores themes of sniper, assassin, berlin,
germany, amnesia, based on novel or book.

21
